# 必考词 Unit08
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit08核心词汇

{{pace}}{{/peɪs}}{{n./v. 步伐；速度；节奏；踱步}}{{The company is growing at a rapid pace.}}
{{pact}}{{/pækt}}{{n. 协定；公约；条约}}{{The two countries signed a trade pact.}}
{{pale}}{{/peɪl}}{{adj. 苍白的；浅色的；无力的}}{{She looked pale after the illness.}}
{{pandemic}}{{/pænˈdemɪk}}{{n./adj. 流行病；大流行的}}{{The pandemic affected millions of people worldwide.}}
{{panel}}{{/ˈpænl}}{{n. 面板；专家组；陪审团}}{{The expert panel discussed the issue at length.}}
{{parallel}}{{/ˈpærəlel}}{{adj./n. 平行的；相似之物；对比}}{{The two roads run parallel to each other.}}
{{paralyze}}{{/ˈpærəlaɪz}}{{v. 使瘫痪；使麻痹；使停顿}}{{The accident paralyzed him from the waist down.}}
{{parcel}}{{/ˈpɑːsl}}{{n. 包裹；一块地；一批}}{{She sent a parcel to her friend abroad.}}
{{partial}}{{/ˈpɑːʃl}}{{adj. 部分的；偏爱的；偏袒的}}{{The project is only a partial success.}}
{{participate}}{{/pɑːˈtɪsɪpeɪt}}{{v. 参加；参与；分享}}{{All students are encouraged to participate in sports.}}
{{particular}}{{/pəˈtɪkjələr}}{{adj. 特定的；讲究的；挑剔的}}{{Is there a particular reason for your absence?}}
{{passion}}{{/ˈpæʃn}}{{n. 热情；激情；酷爱}}{{She has a passion for music.}}
{{passive}}{{/ˈpæsɪv}}{{adj. 被动的；消极的；顺从的}}{{He took a passive role in the discussion.}}
{{patent}}{{/ˈpætnt}}{{n./adj. 专利；明显的；公然的}}{{The company holds several patents for its inventions.}}
{{patience}}{{/ˈpeɪʃns}}{{n. 耐心；忍耐；毅力}}{{Teaching children requires great patience.}}
{{patriotic}}{{/ˌpætriˈɒtɪk}}{{adj. 爱国的；有爱国心的}}{{The patriotic speech moved the audience.}}
{{patron}}{{/ˈpeɪtrən}}{{n. 赞助人；顾客；主顾}}{{The museum has many wealthy patrons.}}
{{pattern}}{{/ˈpætn}}{{n. 模式；图案；样式；典范}}{{The pattern of behavior is hard to change.}}
{{peak}}{{/piːk}}{{n./adj. 顶峰；最高的；高峰的}}{{The company reached its peak in 2019.}}
{{peculiar}}{{/pɪˈkjuːliər}}{{adj. 独特的；奇怪的；特有的}}{{There was a peculiar smell in the room.}}
{{peer}}{{/pɪər}}{{n./v. 同龄人；同辈；凝视}}{{She is respected by her peers.}}
{{penalty}}{{/ˈpenəlti}}{{n. 惩罚；罚款；刑罚}}{{The penalty for speeding is a heavy fine.}}
{{penetrate}}{{/ˈpenɪtreɪt}}{{v. 穿透；渗入；洞察；进入}}{{The cold wind penetrated through the thin jacket.}}
{{pension}}{{/ˈpenʃn}}{{n. 养老金；退休金；抚恤金}}{{The government increased the pension for the elderly.}}
{{perceive}}{{/pəˈsiːv}}{{v. 察觉；理解；认为；感知}}{{She perceived a change in his attitude.}}
{{percentage}}{{/pəˈsentɪdʒ}}{{n. 百分比；比例；部分}}{{A large percentage of the population lives in cities.}}
{{perception}}{{/pəˈsepʃn}}{{n. 感知；认识；看法；洞察力}}{{Public perception of the company has improved.}}
{{perform}}{{/pəˈfɔːm}}{{v. 执行；表演；表现；运行}}{{The students performed well in the exam.}}
{{periodic}}{{/ˌpɪəriˈɒdɪk}}{{adj. 周期的；定期的；间歇的}}{{The company conducts periodic reviews of its policies.}}
{{permanent}}{{/ˈpɜːmənənt}}{{adj. 永久的；持久的；常设的}}{{She found a permanent job in the city.}}
{{permit}}{{/pəˈmɪt}}{{v./n. 允许；许可证；执照}}{{Smoking is not permitted in this building.}}
{{persist}}{{/pəˈsɪst}}{{v. 坚持；持续；固执己见}}{{She persisted in her efforts despite the difficulties.}}
{{personal}}{{/ˈpɜːsənl}}{{adj. 个人的；私人的；亲自的}}{{Please do not ask personal questions.}}
{{perspective}}{{/pəˈspektɪv}}{{n. 观点；视角；远景；透视}}{{Let's look at the issue from a different perspective.}}
{{persuade}}{{/pəˈsweɪd}}{{v. 说服；劝说；使相信}}{{She persuaded him to change his mind.}}
{{petition}}{{/pəˈtɪʃn}}{{n./v. 请愿；请愿书；祈求}}{{The citizens signed a petition against the new law.}}
{{phase}}{{/feɪz}}{{n. 阶段；时期；相位；方面}}{{The project is in its final phase.}}
{{phenomenon}}{{/fɪˈnɒmɪnən}}{{n. 现象；奇才；杰出的人}}{{Global warming is a well-known phenomenon.}}
{{philosophy}}{{/fɪˈlɒsəfi}}{{n. 哲学；人生观；原理}}{{He studied philosophy at university.}}
{{physical}}{{/ˈfɪzɪkl}}{{adj. 身体的；物理的；物质的}}{{Physical exercise is important for health.}}
{{pioneer}}{{/ˌpaɪəˈnɪər}}{{n./v. 先驱；开拓者；开创}}{{She was a pioneer in the field of genetics.}}
{{plague}}{{/pleɪɡ}}{{n./v. 瘟疫；灾祸；使苦恼；烦扰}}{{The country was plagued by corruption.}}
{{platform}}{{/ˈplætfɔːm}}{{n. 平台；站台；讲台；纲领}}{{The train arrived at platform 3.}}
{{plausible}}{{/ˈplɔːzəbl}}{{adj. 似乎合理的；貌似可信的}}{{His explanation sounds plausible.}}
{{plead}}{{/pliːd}}{{v. 恳求；辩护；以…为理由}}{{He pleaded not guilty in court.}}
{{pledge}}{{/pledʒ}}{{n./v. 誓言；保证；抵押；承诺}}{{He pledged to donate half of his wealth to charity.}}
{{plot}}{{/plɒt}}{{n./v. 情节；阴谋；策划；标绘}}{{The novel has a complicated plot.}}
{{plug}}{{/plʌɡ}}{{n./v. 插头；塞子；堵塞；宣传}}{{She plugged in the charger and waited.}}
{{plunge}}{{/plʌndʒ}}{{v./n. 跳入；骤降；暴跌；投身}}{{Stock prices plunged after the announcement.}}
{{plus}}{{/plʌs}}{{prep./n./adj. 加；优势；正的；好的}}{{The job requires experience plus a degree.}}
{{pointed}}{{/ˈpɔɪntɪd}}{{adj. 尖锐的；有针对性的；尖的}}{{She made a pointed remark about his absence.}}
{{poison}}{{/ˈpɔɪzn}}{{n./v. 毒药；毒害；污染；败坏}}{{The water was contaminated with poison.}}
{{policy}}{{/ˈpɒləsi}}{{n. 政策；方针；保险单}}{{The government introduced a new education policy.}}
{{polish}}{{/ˈpɒlɪʃ}}{{v./n. 擦亮；润色；磨光；优雅}}{{She polished the silver until it shone.}}
{{political}}{{/pəˈlɪtɪkl}}{{adj. 政治的；政党的；关心政治的}}{{Political stability is essential for economic growth.}}
{{poll}}{{/pəʊl}}{{n./v. 民意调查；投票；得票}}{{The latest poll shows the candidate is leading.}}
{{pollution}}{{/pəˈluːʃn}}{{n. 污染；污染物；玷污}}{{Air pollution is a serious problem in many cities.}}
{{ponder}}{{/ˈpɒndər}}{{v. 沉思；考虑；深思熟虑}}{{She pondered the question for a long time.}}
{{popular}}{{/ˈpɒpjələr}}{{adj. 受欢迎的；流行的；大众的}}{{The song became very popular among young people.}}
{{populate}}{{/ˈpɒpjuleɪt}}{{v. 居住于；构成人口；殖民于}}{{The island is populated by about 500 families.}}
{{portable}}{{/ˈpɔːtəbl}}{{adj. 便携的；手提的；轻便的}}{{A portable computer is convenient for travel.}}
{{portion}}{{/ˈpɔːʃn}}{{n. 部分；一份；一客}}{{She ate a small portion of the cake.}}
{{portrait}}{{/ˈpɔːtrɪt}}{{n. 肖像；画像；描述；写照}}{{The artist painted a portrait of the queen.}}
{{pose}}{{/pəʊz}}{{v./n. 摆姿势；造成；提出；姿态；假装}}{{The new policy poses a challenge for small businesses.}}
{{positive}}{{/ˈpɒzətɪv}}{{adj. 积极的；肯定的；正的；阳性的}}{{A positive attitude can lead to success.}}
{{possess}}{{/pəˈzes}}{{v. 拥有；具有；支配；控制}}{{She possesses great leadership skills.}}
{{postpone}}{{/pəʊstˈpəʊn}}{{v. 推迟；延期；延缓}}{{The meeting was postponed until next week.}}
{{potential}}{{/pəˈtenʃl}}{{adj./n. 潜在的；可能的；潜力；电位}}{{She has the potential to become a great scientist.}}
{{poverty}}{{/ˈpɒvəti}}{{n. 贫穷；贫困；贫乏；低劣}}{{Millions of people still live in poverty.}}
{{practical}}{{/ˈpræktɪkl}}{{adj. 实际的；实用的；实践的；务实的}}{{We need practical solutions, not just theories.}}
{{precede}}{{/prɪˈsiːd}}{{v. 在…之前；先于；高于}}{{The meeting was preceded by a brief reception.}}
{{precious}}{{/ˈpreʃəs}}{{adj. 珍贵的；宝贵的；过分讲究的}}{{Time is the most precious resource we have.}}
{{precise}}{{/prɪˈsaɪs}}{{adj. 精确的；准确的；严谨的}}{{Please give me the precise time of the meeting.}}
{{predict}}{{/prɪˈdɪkt}}{{v. 预测；预言；预报}}{{It is difficult to predict the future of the economy.}}
{{predominant}}{{/prɪˈdɒmɪnənt}}{{adj. 占主导地位的；显著的；主要的}}{{English is the predominant language in business.}}
{{prefer}}{{/prɪˈfɜːr}}{{v. 更喜欢；宁愿；提出}}{{She prefers tea to coffee.}}
{{prejudice}}{{/ˈpredʒudɪs}}{{n./v. 偏见；歧视；损害}}{{Prejudice against minorities is still a problem.}}
{{preliminary}}{{/prɪˈlɪmɪnəri}}{{adj./n. 初步的；预备的；准备工作}}{{The preliminary results are encouraging.}}
{{premise}}{{/ˈpremɪs}}{{n. 前提；房屋；假设}}{{The argument is based on a false premise.}}
{{premium}}{{/ˈpriːmiəm}}{{n./adj. 保险费；额外费用；优质的}}{{Customers pay a premium for organic food.}}
{{prepare}}{{/prɪˈpeər}}{{v. 准备；预备；筹备；调制}}{{She prepared a delicious meal for the guests.}}
{{prescribe}}{{/prɪˈskraɪb}}{{v. 开处方；规定；命令}}{{The doctor prescribed a new medicine for the patient.}}
{{presence}}{{/ˈprezns}}{{n. 存在；出席；风度；仪态}}{{His presence at the meeting was greatly appreciated.}}
{{preserve}}{{/prɪˈzɜːv}}{{v. 保护；保存；保持；维护}}{{We must preserve our cultural heritage.}}
{{press}}{{/pres}}{{v./n. 按；压；新闻界；出版社}}{{The journalist works for the national press.}}
{{pressure}}{{/ˈpreʃər}}{{n. 压力；压迫；压强；催促}}{{Students are under a lot of pressure during exams.}}
{{prestige}}{{/preˈstiːʒ}}{{n. 威望；声望；影响力}}{{The university enjoys international prestige.}}
{{presume}}{{/prɪˈzjuːm}}{{v. 假定；认为；冒昧；擅自行事}}{{I presume you have read the report.}}
{{pretend}}{{/prɪˈtend}}{{v. 假装；佯装；自称；模拟}}{{He pretended to be asleep when I entered the room.}}
{{prevail}}{{/prɪˈveɪl}}{{v. 盛行；获胜；说服；占优势}}{{Justice will prevail in the end.}}
{{prevalent}}{{/ˈprevələnt}}{{adj. 流行的；普遍的；盛行的}}{{Smartphones are prevalent in modern society.}}
{{prevent}}{{/prɪˈvent}}{{v. 预防；阻止；防止；妨碍}}{{Washing hands regularly can prevent the spread of disease.}}
{{previous}}{{/ˈpriːviəs}}{{adj. 以前的；先的；过早的}}{{She had no previous experience in management.}}
{{primary}}{{/ˈpraɪməri}}{{adj. 主要的；初级的；基本的；首要的}}{{Education is the primary concern for most parents.}}
{{prime}}{{/praɪm}}{{adj./n. 首要的；最好的；全盛时期}}{{He is in the prime of his career.}}
{{primitive}}{{/ˈprɪmɪtɪv}}{{adj. 原始的；简陋的；粗糙的}}{{Primitive people lived in caves.}}
{{principle}}{{/ˈprɪnsəpl}}{{n. 原则；原理；准则；道义}}{{He is a man of principle.}}
{{prior}}{{/ˈpraɪər}}{{adj. 在前的；优先的；更重要的}}{{Prior to the meeting, please read the report.}}
{{priority}}{{/praɪˈɒrəti}}{{n. 优先；优先事项；重点}}{{Safety is our top priority.}}
{{privilege}}{{/ˈprɪvəlɪdʒ}}{{n. 特权；荣幸；优惠；特殊待遇}}{{Education is a right, not a privilege.}}
{{probe}}{{/prəʊb}}{{v./n. 探索；调查；探测器；探针}}{{Scientists sent a space probe to Mars.}}
{{proceed}}{{/prəˈsiːd}}{{v. 继续；进行；出发；行进}}{{Please proceed to the next question.}}
{{process}}{{/ˈprəʊses}}{{n./v. 过程；加工；处理；诉讼程序}}{{The process of learning takes time and effort.}}
{{proclaim}}{{/prəˈkleɪm}}{{v. 宣布；声明；表明；显示}}{{The president proclaimed a state of emergency.}}
{{productive}}{{/prəˈdʌktɪv}}{{adj. 多产的；富有成效的；生产性的}}{{She had a very productive meeting with the team.}}
{{profession}}{{/prəˈfeʃn}}{{n. 职业；行业；同行；声明}}{{Teaching is a noble profession.}}
{{proficient}}{{/prəˈfɪʃnt}}{{adj. 熟练的；精通的；擅长的}}{{She is proficient in both English and French.}}
{{profit}}{{/ˈprɒfɪt}}{{n./v. 利润；益处；获益；获利}}{{The company made a large profit this year.}}
{{profound}}{{/prəˈfaʊnd}}{{adj. 深刻的；深远的；渊博的；深切的}}{{The book had a profound impact on my thinking.}}
{{prohibit}}{{/prəˈhɪbɪt}}{{v. 禁止；阻止；妨碍；使不可能}}{{The law prohibits the sale of alcohol to minors.}}
{{project}}{{/ˈprɒdʒekt}}{{n./v. 项目；计划；投射；预测；放映}}{{The construction project will take two years to complete.}}
{{prominent}}{{/ˈprɒmɪnənt}}{{adj. 突出的；著名的；显著的；杰出的}}{{She is a prominent figure in the field of medicine.}}
{{promote}}{{/prəˈməʊt}}{{v. 促进；晋升；推销；倡议}}{{The company promoted him to senior manager.}}
{{prompt}}{{/prɒmpt}}{{adj./v. 迅速的；及时的；促使；提示}}{{The news prompted a public debate.}}
{{proof}}{{/pruːf}}{{n. 证据；证明；检验；校样}}{{There is no proof that he committed the crime.}}
{{propaganda}}{{/ˌprɒpəˈɡændə}}{{n. 宣传；鼓吹；宣传运动}}{{The government used propaganda to influence public opinion.}}
{{property}}{{/ˈprɒpəti}}{{n. 财产；房地产；性质；所有权}}{{The property market has been booming.}}
{{proportion}}{{/prəˈpɔːʃn}}{{n. 比例；部分；均衡；相称}}{{A large proportion of the budget goes to education.}}
{{propose}}{{/prəˈpəʊz}}{{v. 提议；建议；求婚；打算}}{{He proposed a new plan for the project.}}
{{prospect}}{{/ˈprɒspekt}}{{n. 前景；展望；可能性；景色}}{{The job offers good career prospects.}}
{{prospective}}{{/prəˈspektɪv}}{{adj. 预期的；潜在的；未来的}}{{The company is interviewing prospective candidates.}}
{{prosperity}}{{/prɒˈsperəti}}{{n. 繁荣；兴旺；成功；幸运}}{{The country enjoyed a period of prosperity.}}
{{protect}}{{/prəˈtekt}}{{v. 保护；防护；保险；关税保护}}{{Sunscreen protects your skin from UV rays.}}
{{protest}}{{/ˈprəʊtest}}{{n./v. 抗议；反对；申明；拒付}}{{Thousands joined the protest against the new law.}}
{{prove}}{{/pruːv}}{{v. 证明；证实；检验；结果是}}{{The experiment proved the theory correct.}}
{{provide}}{{/prəˈvaɪd}}{{v. 提供；供应；规定；装备}}{{The hotel provides free Wi-Fi for guests.}}
{{provoke}}{{/prəˈvəʊk}}{{v. 激怒；引起；挑衅；驱使}}{{His remarks provoked anger among the audience.}}
{{psychological}}{{/ˌsaɪkəˈlɒdʒɪkl}}{{adj. 心理的；心理学的；精神的}}{{The event had a deep psychological impact on the survivors.}}
{{publication}}{{/ˌpʌblɪˈkeɪʃn}}{{n. 出版物；出版；发表；公布}}{{The publication of the book was delayed.}}
{{publish}}{{/ˈpʌblɪʃ}}{{v. 出版；发表；公布；发行}}{{The journal published her research paper.}}
{{punish}}{{/ˈpʌnɪʃ}}{{v. 惩罚；处罚；严厉对待}}{{The law punishes those who break the rules.}}
{{purchase}}{{/ˈpɜːtʃəs}}{{v./n. 购买；购置；购买的东西}}{{She purchased a new laptop online.}}
{{pure}}{{/pjʊər}}{{adj. 纯的；纯洁的；纯粹的；完全的}}{{The water in the mountain stream is very pure.}}
{{purpose}}{{/ˈpɜːpəs}}{{n. 目的；用途；决心；意义}}{{The purpose of the meeting is to discuss the budget.}}
{{pursue}}{{/pəˈsjuː}}{{v. 追求；追赶；从事；继续}}{{She pursued a career in medicine.}}
{{qualify}}{{/ˈkwɒlɪfaɪ}}{{v. 使合格；具有资格；限定；修饰}}{{Her experience qualifies her for the position.}}
{{radical}}{{/ˈrædɪkl}}{{adj./n. 激进的；根本的；彻底的；激进分子}}{{The government introduced radical reforms.}}
{{random}}{{/ˈrændəm}}{{adj. 随机的；任意的；胡乱的}}{{The numbers were selected at random.}}
{{range}}{{/reɪndʒ}}{{n./v. 范围；山脉；排列；变化；射程}}{{The store offers a wide range of products.}}
{{rank}}{{/ræŋk}}{{n./v. 等级；排名；排列；列为}}{{The university ranks among the top 10 in the world.}}
{{rational}}{{/ˈræʃnəl}}{{adj. 理性的；合理的；理智的}}{{We need to make rational decisions.}}
{{raw}}{{/rɔː}}{{adj. 生的；未加工的；原始的；擦破皮的}}{{The factory imports raw materials from abroad.}}
{{react}}{{/riˈækt}}{{v. 反应；起化学反应；反抗}}{{How did she react to the news?}}
{{realistic}}{{/ˌriːəˈlɪstɪk}}{{adj. 现实的；逼真的；实际可行的}}{{We should set realistic goals.}}
{{realm}}{{/relm}}{{n. 领域；王国；范围；领地}}{{She made important contributions to the realm of science.}}
{{reasonable}}{{/ˈriːznəbl}}{{adj. 合理的；公道的；通情达理的}}{{The price is very reasonable for the quality.}}
{{rebel}}{{/ˈrebl}}{{n./v. 叛乱者；反抗；叛逆}}{{The rebels fought against the government.}}
{{recall}}{{/rɪˈkɔːl}}{{v./n. 回忆；召回；收回；记忆力}}{{I can't recall where I put my keys.}}
{{recover}}{{/rɪˈkʌvər}}{{v. 恢复；收回；弥补；痊愈}}{{She has fully recovered from her illness.}}
{{recruit}}{{/rɪˈkruːt}}{{v./n. 招聘；新成员；招募；吸收}}{{The company is recruiting new graduates.}}
{{reduce}}{{/rɪˈdjuːs}}{{v. 减少；降低；缩小；简化}}{{The company reduced its workforce by 10%.}}
{{refer}}{{/rɪˈfɜːr}}{{v. 提到；参考；转介；查阅}}{{Please refer to the handbook for details.}}
{{reflect}}{{/rɪˈflekt}}{{v. 反映；反射；思考；反省}}{{The lake reflected the mountains beautifully.}}
{{reform}}{{/rɪˈfɔːm}}{{n./v. 改革；改良；改正；革新}}{{The education reform aims to improve teaching quality.}}
{{regard}}{{/rɪˈɡɑːd}}{{v./n. 看待；尊重；方面；问候}}{{He is highly regarded in his field.}}
{{region}}{{/ˈriːdʒən}}{{n. 地区；区域；范围；部位}}{{The tropical region has a warm climate all year.}}
{{register}}{{/ˈredʒɪstər}}{{v./n. 登记；注册；记录；挂号}}{{She registered for the online course.}}
{{regulate}}{{/ˈreɡjuleɪt}}{{v. 管理；调节；规范；控制}}{{The government regulates the financial industry.}}
{{reject}}{{/rɪˈdʒekt}}{{v. 拒绝；驳回；排斥；丢弃}}{{The committee rejected the proposal.}}
{{relate}}{{/rɪˈleɪt}}{{v. 与…有关；叙述；使有联系；认同}}{{The article relates to the current economic situation.}}
{{release}}{{/rɪˈliːs}}{{v./n. 释放；发行；发布；排放；解脱}}{{The movie will be released next month.}}
{{relevant}}{{/ˈreləvənt}}{{adj. 相关的；切题的；有价值的；有意义的}}{{Please provide relevant documents for the application.}}
{{reliable}}{{/rɪˈlaɪəbl}}{{adj. 可靠的；可信赖的；真实的}}{{She is a reliable colleague.}}
{{reluctant}}{{/rɪˈlʌktənt}}{{adj. 不情愿的；勉强的；犹豫的}}{{He was reluctant to admit his mistake.}}
{{rely}}{{/rɪˈlaɪ}}{{v. 依赖；依靠；信赖；指望}}{{You can rely on me for support.}}
{{remain}}{{/rɪˈmeɪn}}{{v. 保持；剩余；留下；继续存在}}{{The door remained open throughout the night.}}
{{remark}}{{/rɪˈmɑːk}}{{n./v. 评论；谈论；注意到；觉察}}{{She made a remark about the weather.}}
{{remote}}{{/rɪˈməʊt}}{{adj. 遥远的；偏僻的；关系疏远的；微小的}}{{The village is in a remote area of the country.}}
{{render}}{{/ˈrendər}}{{v. 使成为；提供；呈递；表达；粉刷}}{{The accident rendered him unconscious.}}
{{renew}}{{/rɪˈnjuː}}{{v. 更新；续期；恢复；重新开始}}{{She renewed her passport before the trip.}}
{{represent}}{{/ˌreprɪˈzent}}{{v. 代表；象征；表示；描述；代理}}{{The dove represents peace.}}
{{reputation}}{{/ˌrepjuˈteɪʃn}}{{n. 名誉；声望；名声；信誉}}{{The company has a good reputation for quality.}}
{{request}}{{/rɪˈkwest}}{{n./v. 请求；要求；邀请；需要}}{{She made a request for more time.}}
{{require}}{{/rɪˈkwaɪər}}{{v. 需要；要求；命令；规定}}{{The job requires strong communication skills.}}
{{rescue}}{{/ˈreskjuː}}{{v./n. 营救；解救；挽救；救援行动}}{{The firefighters rescued the trapped passengers.}}
{{research}}{{/rɪˈsɜːtʃ}}{{n./v. 研究；调查；探索；学术研究}}{{The research was conducted over three years.}}
{{resemble}}{{/rɪˈzembl}}{{v. 像；类似于；与…相似}}{{She resembles her mother in many ways.}}
{{reserve}}{{/rɪˈzɜːv}}{{v./n. 保留；预订；储备；保护区；矜持}}{{I'd like to reserve a table for two.}}
{{reside}}{{/rɪˈzaɪd}}{{v. 居住；定居；存在于；属于}}{{She resides in a small town near the coast.}}
{{resign}}{{/rɪˈzaɪn}}{{v. 辞职；放弃；使顺从；委托}}{{He resigned from his position as CEO.}}
{{resist}}{{/rɪˈzɪst}}{{v. 抵抗；抵制；忍住；抗拒}}{{The material resists heat and water.}}
{{resolve}}{{/rɪˈzɒlv}}{{v./n. 解决；决心；决定；分解}}{{They resolved the conflict through negotiation.}}
{{resort}}{{/rɪˈzɔːt}}{{n./v. 度假胜地；求助于；诉诸；凭借}}{{The beach resort is popular with tourists.}}
{{resource}}{{/rɪˈsɔːs}}{{n. 资源；办法；财力；智谋}}{{We must use our natural resources wisely.}}
{{respond}}{{/rɪˈspɒnd}}{{v. 回答；反应；响应；回报}}{{She responded quickly to the emergency.}}
{{responsible}}{{/rɪˈspɒnsəbl}}{{adj. 负责的；有责任心的；可靠的}}{{Who is responsible for this mess?}}
{{restore}}{{/rɪˈstɔːr}}{{v. 恢复；修复；归还；重建}}{{The old painting was carefully restored.}}
{{restrict}}{{/rɪˈstrɪkt}}{{v. 限制；约束；限定；束缚}}{{Access to the area is restricted.}}
{{retain}}{{/rɪˈteɪn}}{{v. 保持；保留；记住；聘请}}{{The company retained all its employees.}}
{{reveal}}{{/rɪˈviːl}}{{v. 揭示；透露；显示；展现}}{{The investigation revealed surprising facts.}}
{{revenue}}{{/ˈrevənjuː}}{{n. 收入；税收；收益；税务局}}{{The company's revenue increased by 20%.}}
{{reverse}}{{/rɪˈvɜːs}}{{v./adj./n. 颠倒；相反的；背面；逆转；倒退}}{{The court reversed the decision.}}
{{review}}{{/rɪˈvjuː}}{{v./n. 审查；评论；复习；检阅；回顾}}{{The professor reviewed the students' papers.}}
{{revise}}{{/rɪˈvaɪz}}{{v. 修订；修改；复习；改变}}{{She revised her essay before submitting it.}}
{{revive}}{{/rɪˈvaɪv}}{{v. 复兴；恢复；苏醒；重演}}{{The government aims to revive the economy.}}
{{revolution}}{{/ˌrevəˈluːʃn}}{{n. 革命；旋转；彻底变革；循环}}{{The industrial revolution transformed society.}}
{{reward}}{{/rɪˈwɔːd}}{{n./v. 奖赏；报酬；回报；酬谢}}{{Hard work will eventually bring its reward.}}
{{rival}}{{/ˈraɪvl}}{{n./adj./v. 竞争对手；竞争的；与…匹敌}}{{The two companies have been rivals for years.}}
{{rob}}{{/rɒb}}{{v. 抢劫；剥夺；使丧失}}{{The bank was robbed last night.}}
{{role}}{{/rəʊl}}{{n. 角色；作用；任务；职责}}{{Education plays a key role in personal development.}}
{{root}}{{/ruːt}}{{n. 根；根源；基础；词根}}{{The root of the problem is lack of communication.}}
{{rough}}{{/rʌf}}{{adj. 粗糙的；大致的；艰难的；粗暴的}}{{The road was rough and hard to drive on.}}
{{routine}}{{/ruːˈtiːn}}{{n./adj. 常规；日常的；例行的；平淡的}}{{Exercise is part of her daily routine.}}
{{royal}}{{/ˈrɔɪəl}}{{adj. 王室的；皇家的；盛大的；一流的}}{{The royal family attended the ceremony.}}
{{ruin}}{{/ˈruːɪn}}{{v./n. 毁灭；废墟；破产；毁坏}}{{The earthquake ruined many historic buildings.}}
{{rural}}{{/ˈrʊərəl}}{{adj. 农村的；乡下的；田园的}}{{Rural areas often lack access to healthcare.}}
{{rush}}{{/rʌʃ}}{{v./n. 冲；急忙；高峰期；抢购}}{{Everyone rushed to the exit when the alarm sounded.}}
